course: dictionary
lesson: 9988
title: Technique: the right way to do it
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A technique is a special way of doing something that takes skill. It is a method, a set of moves or steps that helps you do a task well. «Reading like a writer means noticing the techniques authors use so that you can use them too.» Here, techniques are the tricks writers use, like a strong opening or vivid description.
explain: Technique can also mean how well you use those moves. In a football match, a player may score because of good technique: the right foot placement, a smooth swing and a firm strike. Good technique is about using the right method well, not about luck.
explain: Look for clue words around it. Phrases like «good technique», «learn a technique» and «breathing technique» tell you it is a way of doing something. To check your meaning, swap in "way of doing it" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A technique is a special way of doing something that needs skill.
fact: Technique can mean the right moves or methods used well in a sport, art or job.
fact: In PE, coaches teach the right technique for throwing, jumping or swimming.
fact: In science, lab techniques must be followed safely.
fact: Counting breaths from one to ten and starting again is an old meditation technique.
exercise: «Reading like a writer means noticing the techniques authors use.» What is a technique here? | *A special way of doing something that needs skill | A list of words for a spelling test | A type of book with a hard cover | A kind of lunch
exercise: In PE, coaches teach the right technique for throwing. What does technique mean here? | The place where the ball lands | The score at the end of the game | *The right moves for doing it well | The name of the coach
exercise: In maths, pupils learn techniques such as column addition. Which of these is a technique? | The classroom door | *Column addition, a set method for adding numbers | The number seven | A pencil case
test: «Maya's next shot flies into the top corner», and the reason is good technique. What does technique mean here? | Wearing new boots | Standing very still | *The right moves and methods used well | Pure luck with no practice
test: What does «breathing technique» most likely mean? | *A special method for breathing | A type of cloud | A breath of fresh air | The speed of a runner
exam: Which sentence uses technique correctly? | The painter put the technique in the bin. | The painter ate a technique for lunch. | *The painter used a shading technique to make the apple look round. | The painter's technique was the colour of the sky.
